==== 原文

#@# 英文は原本の組版上の行末で改行せず、段落・宛名・署名などの区切りのみ保った。行末のハイフンによる分綴は戻した。
#@# [要確認: 原本「picty」は「piety」の誤植と思はれるが、原本のまま]
Dear Child—Although we are separated in person, yet you are never absent from my thoughts; and it is my continual practice to recommend you to the care of that Being, whose eyes are on all his creatures, and to whom the secrets of all hearts are open; but I have been lately somewhat alarmed, because your two last letters do not run in that strain of unaffected picty as formerly. What, my dear, is this owing to? does virtue appear to you unpleasant, is your beneficent Creator a hard master, or are you resolved to embark in the fashionable follies of a gay, unthinking world? Excuse me, my dear, I am a mother, and my concern for your happiness is inseparably connected with my own. Perhaps I am mistaken, and what I have considered as a fault may be only the effusions of youthful gaiety.—I shall consider it in that light, and be extremely glad, yea happy to find it so. Useful instructions are never too often inculcated, and therefore, give me leave again to put you in mind of that duty, the performance of which alone can make you happy, both in time and in eternity.

Religion, my dear, is the dedication of the whole mind to the will of God, and virtue is the actual operation of that truth which diffuses itself through every part of our conduct; its consequences are equally beneficial as its promises: “Her ways are ways of pleasantness and all her paths are peace.”

Whilst the gay unthinking part of youth are devoting the whole of their time to fashionable pleasures, how happy shall I be to hear that my child was religious without hypocritical austerity, and even gay with innocence! Let me beg that you will spend at least one hour each day in perusing your Bible, and some of our best English writers; and don't imagine that religion is such a gloomy thing as some enthusiasts have represented: no, it indulges you in every rational amusement, so far as is consistent with morality;—it forbids nothing but what is hurtful.

Let me beg you will consider attentively what I have written, and send me an answer as soon as you can.—I am your affectionate-mother.

=== @<ruby>{同上, どうじやう}に對する娘の@<ruby>{返事, へんじ}

@<ruby>{拜復, はいふく}、
眞に@<ruby>{親君, おやぎみ}としての御情深き@<ruby>{御忠言, ごちうげん}を@<ruby>{熟讀, じゆくどく}いたしては、
御返事認むべき@<ruby>{筆, ふで}も殆ど持ちかね@<ruby>{候程, さふらふほど}に感動いたし候、
されども今は自ら身を@<ruby>{休, やす}ましめんとの@<ruby>{心, こゝろ}@<ruby>{之無, これな}くて候、
何を@<ruby>{措, お}きても御手紙に@<ruby>{御返事, ごへんじ}@<ruby>{參, まゐ}らせ、
御心を@<ruby>{安, やす}んじまゐらせんを眞の親に子たるの@<ruby>{身, み}として當然の@<ruby>{義務, ぎむ}と存候。
過日差上候書中、
@<ruby>{浮薄, ふはく}に@<ruby>{流, なが}れ@<ruby>{候趣, さふらふおもむき}@<ruby>{相見, あひみ}え候は如何にも御尤もにて、
私は之を@<ruby>{否定, ひてい}@<ruby>{致, いた}しかね候。
自らその@<ruby>{愚, ぐ}を@<ruby>{蔽, おほ}はんとも願ひ申さず、
心より@<ruby>{白狀, はくじやう}いたし候。
されども、
只右の@<ruby>{手紙, てがみ}は私の@<ruby>{誠, まこと}の@<ruby>{心, こゝろ}を@<ruby>{顯, あらは}したるにても無之、
只不注意に@<ruby>{如何, いか}なる人に@<ruby>{對, たい}して發し候かをも考へずして、
@<ruby>{認, した}ゝめ候ものなることを@<ruby>{相, あひ}@<ruby>{述, の}べ申度候、
これ@<ruby>{僞, いつはり}なき私の@<ruby>{心, こゝろ}にて候。
既に深く我が@<ruby>{過, あやまち}を@<ruby>{自覺, じかく}@<ruby>{致候, いたしさふら}へば、
かまへて再び少しにても@<ruby>{御心, おんこゝろ}をそこなひ申すまじく候。
@<ruby>{尊, たふと}き御ふみにて送り給ひし@<ruby>{御忠言, ごちうげん}は、
今更@<ruby>{讃辭, さんじ}を@<ruby>{呈, てい}し候までも之なく、
之を@<ruby>{肝, きも}に@<ruby>{銘, めい}じて@<ruby>{忘, わす}れざらん事、
私が唯一の@<ruby>{願, ねがひ}にて候。
@<ruby>{懷, なつか}しき母樣よ、
私は宗敎を@<ruby>{愛, あい}し@<ruby>{德, とく}を愛し申候、
如何なる@<ruby>{事由, じいう}も此義務の@<ruby>{遂行, すゐかう}を@<ruby>{妨, さまた}ぐるもの@<ruby>{可無之, これなかるべく}、
@<ruby>{偏, ひとへ}に望み居候。
何卒折々御手紙賜り度、
又@<ruby>{將來, しやうらい}の@<ruby>{行爲, かうゐ}を以て、
數ある@<ruby>{人, ひと}の親の中に、
@<ruby>{眞, しん}の@<ruby>{親, おや}たる母上樣の御望み@<ruby>{遊, あそ}ばされ候樣なる人間なりと@<ruby>{證明, しようめい}いたしたき@<ruby>{希望, きばう}に@<ruby>{御座, ござ}@<ruby>{候, さふらふ}。
謹言。

