==== 原文

#@# [要確認: 原本「thlng」「strects」「danghter」は誤植と思はれるが、原本のまま]
Dear Mother,—It is now a month that I have been at Mr. Wilson's and I thank God that I like my place very well. My master and mistress are both worthy people, and greatly respected by all their neighbours. At my first coming here I thought every thlng strange, and wondered to see such multitudes of people in the strects; but what I suffer most from is, the remembrance of your's and my father's kindness: but I begin to be more reconciled to my state, as I know you were not able to support me at home. I return you a thousand thanks for the kind advice you were so good to give me at parting, and I shall endeavour to practise it as long as I live: Let me hear from you as often as you have an opportunity; so with my duty to you and my father, and kind love to all friends,

//flushright{
I remain, your most dutiful danghter.
//}

