My dear Mrs. Green,

Will you give us the pleasure of your company for a few day's visit while town is so full of attractions? Can you come on the 16th, and stay till the 24th? We could do a couple of theatres together, and see some of the exhibitions of pictures. We are lookiing forward to taking you on one or two motoring expeditions, and Sir Archibald asks me to tell you that he is waiting to fix the date of a river party he is planning, until he hears if you can join it. We both hope you will be able to come to us.

//flushright{
Very Sincerely Yours,@<br>{}Esther Grey.
//}

