#@# 原本欄外に、(1)〜(3)は「略式」、(4)以下は「正式」とある。
#@# [要確認: 原本「pleasue」は「pleasure」の誤植と思はれるが、原本のまま]
（1）Dear Mrs. Toda,

Will you give us the pleasue of lunching with us on Tuesday July twenty seventh at one o'clock?

//flushright{
Very Truly Yours@<br>{}M. Watanabe.
//}

（2）Dear Mr. and Mrs. Toda,

Will you and Dr. Toda give us the pleasure to lunch with us at Fujimiken, on Thursday July 27th at 2o'clock? Mr. and Mrs. C. from America will be our party and I am asking our mutual friends Mr. and Mrs. K. and Miss S.

//flushright{
Very Sincerely Yours@<br>{}M. Watanabe,
//}

（3）Dear Mrs. Watanabe,

Many thanks for your kind invitation to lunch on the 18th inst. We accept it with much pleasure.

//flushright{
Yours Very Sincerely@<br>{}E. K. Toda.
//}

（4）Mrs. Alfred E. Buck requests the pleasure of Madam Toda's company at luncheon at the Imperial Hotel on Tuesday October ninth at one o'clock.

//noindent
Oct. 9@<sup>{th.} 1906@<br>{}R. S. V. P.

（5）Mrs. Toda accepts with much pleasure the kind invitation of Mrs. Buck for luncheon on Tuesday October ninth at one o'clock.

（6）Mr. and Mrs. Toda accept with much pleasure Mrs. Buck's kind invitation to lunch with her on Tuesday.

（7）Mrs. Toda regrets that intended absence from town will prevent her accepting Madam Watanabe's kind invitation for luncheon on Tuesday at the Imperial Hotel.

（8）Mrs. Toda thanks Mrs. Watanabe for her kind invitation to lunch on Tuesday but regrets that a previous engagement will deprive her of the pleasure of accepting it.

